nsformUrl\":false,\"matchedKeywords\":[],\"keywords\":\"news, court-and-crime, hot cross buns, over the limit, easter, crookwell police, breathalyser, police, breath test, random breath test\",\"elements\":[{\"colourMode\":\"RGB\",\"cropConfig\":{\"cropHeight\":3095,\"cropWidth\":3024,\"cropX\":0,\"cropY\":0,\"focalX\":1512,\"focalY\":1548,\"scale\":1},\"description\":\"\",\"height\":3095,\"link\":\"\",\"title\":\"\",\"type\":\"image\",\"uri\":\"/mD2CAtAW6YCRaRgZjfziq9/d6bdc523-c2d7-4d4c-a07a-01a0a17da45a.jpg\",\"visible\":[\"web\",\"print\"],\"width\":3024},{\"text\":\"Drivers across the region are being warned to be cautious when consuming their favourite Easter treat.\",\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"text\":\"The yeast in hot cross buns can ferment its various sugars enough for ‘alcohol’ to register on a passive\u0026nbsp;roadside alcometer test.\",\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"text\":\"However, this does not mean it would put a driver over the limit, following further\u0026nbsp;breath analysis procedures.\",\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"text\":\"Last week,\u0026nbsp;a Pilbara truck driver, Heather Jones, blew 0.018 on an alcometer after a mouthful of a such a bun.\u003cbr\u003e\",\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"text\":\"Her video went viral on social media,\u0026nbsp;warning other truck drivers\u0026nbsp;about her results. For a professional driver, such as a truck driver, the legal blood alcohol limit is 0.02.\",\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"text\":\"Inspector Alison Brennan of Hume Police District confirmed that foods and substances other than alcoholic drink could register on the passive roadside breath test device.\u003cbr\u003e\",\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"text\":\"She explained how such a situation could occur.\",\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"text\":\"“In training to become a breath analysis operator, we test all sorts of stuff,” she said, “from mouth wash to garlic to all sorts of things, to see if they will register.\",\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"text\":\"“There are foods and substances that can give a reading on a passive roadside test, but this is exactly why we have these procedures so there can be no doubt,” she said.\u003cbr\u003e\",\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"text\":\"The procedure is\u0026nbsp;a\u0026nbsp;passive test using the alcometer, where a driver speaks into a hand-held device.\u003cbr\u003e\",\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"text\":\"If the\u0026nbsp;alcometer\u0026nbsp;indicates that alcohol is present, the police then attach a tube to the hand-held device to get a sample of air from the driver’s lungs, not their mouth.\u003cbr\u003e\",\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"text\":\"At that point, the ferment of a hot cross bun, for example, should not register an alcoholic\u0026nbsp;reading.\",\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"text\":\"However, if alcohol was present and over the legal limit, the police would then detain the driver and attend the nearest police station.\",\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"text\":\"At the police station,\u0026nbsp;a 15-minute observation period should ensure no residual mouth alcohol in a reading.\u003cbr\u003e\",\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"text\":\"The driver would then be tested on the breath analysis machine, Inspector Brennan said, adding it had “a margin of error so negligible as to be irrefutable”.\",\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"text\":\"Other positive readings in a passive roadside test could be caused by\u0026nbsp;alcohol-based hand wash, an inebriated passenger breathing heavily, strong perfume, or liquor-flavoured desserts.\",\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"text\":\"But as with the hot cross bun, these should not register beyond the initial passive breath test on the roadside.\",\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"items\":[\"\u003cb\u003eREAD ALSO: \u003ca href=\\\"https://www.centralwesterndaily.com.au/story/5861035/police-search-for-four-people-after-reports-of-shots-fired-in-park/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\"\u003ePolice search for four people after reports of shots fired in park\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\",\"\u003cb\u003eREAD ALSO: \u003ca href=\\\"https://www.centralwesterndaily.com.au/story/5863217/residents-warned-after-algal-blooms-found-in-molongs-town-water-dam/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\"\u003eResidents warned after algal blooms found in Molong’s town water dam\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\",\"\u003cb\u003eREAD ALSO: \u003ca href=\\\"https://www.centralwesterndaily.com.au/story/5860789/car-fires-another-vehicle-set-alight-in-cootes-park-video/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\"\u003eCar fires: Another vehicle set alight in Cootes Park | Video\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\"],\"listType\":\"unordered\",\"type\":\"list\"},{\"text\":\"Brewer\u0026nbsp;Andy Orrell, of Hairyman Brewery and 30 years’ experience,\u0026nbsp;explained the hot cross bun finding.\",\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"text\":\"He said it was likely the baking yeast had the potential to\u0026nbsp;consume\u0026nbsp;the sugars, which\u0026nbsp;had started fermentation.\",\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"text\":\"The yeast could have fermented the sugars in the milled flour, the fruit, and\u0026nbsp;the sugar glaze, he said.\u003cbr\u003e\",\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"text\":\"“The sugars\u0026nbsp;have been fermented by the yeast, just like beer would have,” he said.\",\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"level\":\"3\",\"text\":\"DO YOU WANT MORE ORANGE NEWS?\",\"type\":\"heading\"},{\"level\":\"3\",\"text\":\"Receive our free newsletters delivered to your inbox, as well as breaking news alerts. Sign up below …\",\"type\":\"heading\"},{\"description\":\"\",\"embed\":\"\u003ciframe height=\\\"850px\\\" src=\\\"https://centralwesterndaily.us15.list-manage.com/subscribe/post?u=3d952e1160da384a612b2b972\u0026amp;id=4e36a4267c\u0026amp;group[2301][1]=1\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\"\u003e\u003c/iframe\u003e\",\"service\":\"iframe\",\"serviceId\":\"\",\"serviceType\":\"iframe\",\"title\":\"IFrame\",\"type\":\"generic\"}],\"seoTitle\":\"Fermenting sugars enough for ‘alcohol’ to register on a passive roadside test\",\"seoDescription\":\"\",\"orgName\":\"Central We